    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The tax-software company's chief executive announced a corporate repositioning to forge a new creative engine around AI, a strategic pivot that will see roughly 17% of its workforce cut. In a painful but necessary reinvention, the maker abandoned thousands of human components, offering a severance package to those displaced. Legacy workshops in Reno and Woodland Hills are being decommissioned as the organization recenters for accelerated production, a stark organizational change that reveals the human cost of redesigning a corporate blueprint.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Creator",
